Cell[BoxData[
 TabViewBox[{{1,"1"->
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"1909.11100\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Hasmik Poghosyan Mrs\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Davide Fioravanti, Hasmik Poghosyan and Rubik Poghossian\
\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"$T$, $Q$ and periods in $SU(3)$ ${\\\\cal N}=2$ \
SYM\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"20 pages, minor corrections, references added\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP03(2020)049\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We consider the third order differential equation \
derived from the deformed\\nSeiberg-Witten differential for pure ${\\\\cal \
N}=2$ SYM with gauge group $SU(3)$\\nin Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit of \
$\\\\Omega$-background. We show that this is the\\nsame differential equation \
that emerges in the context of Ordinary Differential\\nEquation/Integrable \
Models (ODI/IM) correspondence for $2d$ $A_2$ Toda CFT with\\ncentral charge \
$c=98$. We derive the corresponding $QQ$ and related $TQ$\\nfunctional \
relations and establish the asymptotic behaviour of $Q$ and $T$\\nfunctions \
at small instanton parameter $q \\\\rightarrow 0$. Moreover, \
numerical\\nintegration of the Floquet monodromy matrix of the differential \
equation leads\\nto evaluation of the $A$-cycles $a_{1,2,3}$ at any point of \
the moduli space of\\nvacua parametrised by the vector multiplet scalar VEVs \
$\\\\langle\\n\\\\textbf{tr}\\\\,\\\\phi^2\\\\rangle$ and $\\\\langle \
\\\\textbf{tr}\\\\,\\\\phi^3\\\\rangle$ even for\\nlarge values of $q$ which \
are well beyond the reach of instanton calculus. The\\nnumerical results at \
small $q$ are in excellent agreement with instanton\\ncalculation. We \
conjecture a very simple relation between Baxter's $T$-function\\nand \
$A$-cycle periods $a_{1,2,3}$, which is an extension of \
Alexei\\nZamolodchikov's conjecture about Mathieu equation.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Tue, 24 Sep 2019 18:00:06 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v2\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Mon, 28 Oct 2019 17:28:04 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"update_date\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2020-04-22\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors_parsed\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\<\"Fioravanti\"\>", ",", "\<\"Davide\"\>", 
         ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\<\"Poghosyan\"\>", ",", "\<\"Hasmik\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}],
         "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\<\"Poghossian\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rubik\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}],
         "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}, {2,"2"->
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"1910.09406\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Hongfei Shu\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Katsushi Ito and Hongfei Shu\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"TBA equations for the Schr\\\\\\\"odinger equation with \
a regular singularity\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"39 pages, typos corrected\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"J.Phys.A 53 (2020) 33, 335201\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1088/1751-8121/ab96ee\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"TIT/HEP-676, NORDITA 2019-092\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We derive the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) \
equations for the\\nSchr\\\\\\\"odinger equation with an arbitrary polynomial \
potential and a regular\\nsingular (simple and double pole) term. The TBA \
equations provide a non-trivial\\ngeneralization of the ODE/IM correspondence \
and also give a solution for the\\nRiemann-Hilbert problem in the exact WKB \
method. We study the TBA equations in\\ndetail for the linear and the \
harmonic oscillator potentials together with\\ninverse and centrifugal terms. \
As an application, we also compute numerically\\nthe Voros spectrum for these \
potentials using the Bohr-Sommerfeld quantization\\ncondition.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Mon, 21 Oct 2019 14:31:46 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v2\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Tue, 18 Feb 2020 15:45:40 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"update_date\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2021-01-08\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors_parsed\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\<\"Ito\"\>", ",", "\<\"Katsushi\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], 
        "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\<\"Shu\"\>", ",", "\<\"Hongfei\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], 
        "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}, {3,"3"->
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"1911.13290\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Stefano Negro\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Patrick Dorey, Clare Dunning, Stefano Negro, Roberto \
Tateo\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Geometric aspects of the ODE/IM correspondence\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Partially based on lectures given at the Young \
Researchers\\n  Integrability School 2017,in Dublin. 62 pages, 8 figures. \
Minor amendments.\\n  Version published in J. Phys A \\\"Special Issue on \
Recent Advances in AdS/CFT\\n  Integrability\\\"\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. (2020)\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1088/1751-8121/ab83c9\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  This review describes a link between Lax operators, \
embedded surfaces and\\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations for integrable \
quantum field theories.\\nThis surprising connection between classical and \
quantum models is undoubtedly\\none of the most striking discoveries that \
emerged from the off-critical\\ngeneralisation of the ODE/IM correspondence, \
which initially involved only\\nconformal invariant quantum field theories. \
We will mainly focus of the KdV and\\nsinh-Gordon models. However, various \
aspects of other interesting systems, such\\nas affine Toda field theories \
and non-linear sigma models, will be mentioned.\\nWe also discuss the \
implications of these ideas in the AdS/CFT context,\\ninvolving minimal \
surfaces and Wilson loops. This work is a follow-up of the\\nODE/IM review \
published more than ten years ago by JPA, before the discovery of\\nits \
off-critical generalisation and the corresponding \
geometrical\\ninterpretation. (Partially based on lectures given at the Young \
Researchers\\nIntegrability School 2017, in Dublin.)\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Fri, 29 Nov 2019 18:46:27 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v2\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Sat, 14 Dec 2019 18:38:13 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v3\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Fri, 27 Mar 2020 04:12:16 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}]}], 
      "}"}]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"update_date\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2020-03-30\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors_parsed\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\<\"Dorey\"\>", ",", "\<\"Patrick\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], 
        "}"}], ",", 
