   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2105.03777\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Qianyu Hao\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Alba Grassi, Qianyu Hao, Andrew Neitzke\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Exact WKB methods in $SU(2)$ $N_f=1$\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"63 pages, 18 figures\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP01(2022)046\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"UTTG 03-2021, CERN-TH-2021-071\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We study in detail the Schr\\\\\\\"{o}dinger equation \
corresponding to the four\\ndimensional $SU(2)$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SQCD \
theory with one flavour. We calculate\\nthe Voros symbols, or quantum \
periods, in four different ways: Borel summation\\nof the WKB series, direct \
computation of Wronskians of exponentially decaying\\nsolutions, the TBA \
equations of Gaiotto-Moore-Neitzke/Gaiotto, and instanton\\ncounting. We make \
computations by all of these methods, finding good agreement.\\nWe also study \
the exact quantization condition for the spectrum, and we compute\\nthe \
Fredholm determinant of the inverse of the Schr\\\\\\\"odinger operator using \
the\\nTS/ST correspondence and Zamolodchikov's TBA, again finding good \
agreement. In\\naddition, we explore two aspects of the relationship between \
singularities of\\nthe Borel transformed WKB series and BPS states: BPS \
states of the 4d theory\\nare related to singularities in the Borel \
transformed WKB series for the\\nquantum periods, and BPS states of a coupled \
2d+4d system are related to\\nsingularities in the Borel transformed WKB \
series for local solutions of the\\nSchr\\\\\\\"odinger equation.\\n\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
