Jos\\\\`e Francisco\\n  Morales\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"QNMs of branes, BHs and fuzzballs from Quantum SW \
geometries\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"7 pages, 2 figures\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1016/j.physletb.2021.136837\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th astro-ph.HE gr-qc\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  QNMs govern the linear response to perturbations of \
BHs, D-branes and\\nfuzzballs and the gravitational wave signals in the \
ring-down phase of binary\\nmergers. A remarkable connection between QNMs of \
neutral BHs in 4d and quantum\\nSW geometries describing the dynamics of ${\\\
\\cal N}=2$ SYM theories has been\\nrecently put forward. We extend the \
gauge/gravity dictionary to a large class\\nof gravity backgrounds including \
charged and rotating BHs of Einstein-Maxwell\\ntheory in $d=4,5$ dimensions, \
D3-branes, D1D5 `circular' fuzzballs and smooth\\nhorizonless geometries; all \
related to ${\\\\cal N}=2$ SYM with a single $SU(2)$\\ngauge group and \
fundamental matter. We find that photon-spheres, a common\\nfeature of all \
examples, are associated to degenerations of the classical\\nelliptic SW \
geometry whereby a cycle pinches to zero size. Quantum effects\\nresolve the \
singular geometry and lead to a spectrum of quantized energies,\\nlabeled by \
the overtone number $n$. We compute the spectrum of QNMs using exact\\nWKB \
quantization, geodetic motion and numerical simulations and show \
excellent\\nagreement between the three methods. We explicitly illustrate our \
findings for\\nthe case D3-brane QNMs.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
