    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We exploit the recently proposed correspondence \
between gravitational\\nperturbations and quantum Seiberg-Witten curves to \
compute the spectrum of\\nquasi-normal modes of asymptotically flat Kerr \
Newman black holes and establish\\ndetailed gauge/gravity dictionaries for a \
large class of black holes, D-branes\\nand fuzzballs in diverse dimensions. \
QNM frequencies obtained from the quantum\\nperiods of $SU(2)$ ${\\\\cal \
N}=2$ SYM with $N_f=3$ flavours are compared against\\nnumerical results, WKB \
(eikonal) approximation and geodetic motion showing\\nremarkable agreement. \
Starting from the master example relating quasi-normal\\nmodes of Kerr-Newman \
black holes in AdS$_4$ to $SU(2)$ gauge theory with\\n$N_f=4$, we illustrate \
the procedure for some simple toy-models that allow\\nanalytic solutions. We \
also argue that the AGT version of the gauge/gravity\\ncorrespondence may \
give precious hints as to the physical/geometric origin of\\nthe quasi-normal \
modes/Seiberg-Witten connection and further elucidate\\ninteresting \
properties (such as tidal Love numbers and grey-body factors) that\\ncan help \
discriminating black holes from fuzzballs.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
