    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\"\>"}],
     ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We study the WKB periods for the third order ordinary \
differential equation\\n(ODE) with polynomial potential, which is obtained by \
the Nekrasov-Shatashvili\\nlimit of ($A_2,A_N$) Argyres-Douglas theory in the \
Omega background. In the\\nminimal chamber of the moduli space, we derive the \
Y-system and the\\nthermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) equations by using the \
ODE/IM correspondence.\\nThe exact WKB periods are identified with the \
Y-functions. Varying the moduli\\nparameters of the potential, the \
wall-crossing of the TBA equations occurs. We\\nstudy the process of the \
wall-crossing from the minimal chamber to the maximal\\nchamber for \
$(A_2,A_2)$ and $(A_2,A_3)$. When the potential is a monomial type,\\nwe show \
the TBA equations obtained from the ($A_2, A_2$) and ($A_2, A_3$)-type\\nODE \
lead to the $D_4$ and $E_6$-type TBA equations respectively.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
