    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Monserrat Aguayo, Ankai Hern\\\\'andez, Jos\\\\'e Mena, \
Julio Oliva, Marcelo\\n  Oyarzo\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Exact scalar (quasi-)normal modes of black holes and \
solitons in gauged\\n  SUGRA\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"18 pages, 3 figures\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP07(2022)021\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th gr-qc\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  In this paper we identify a new family of black holes \
and solitons that lead\\nto the exact integration of scalar probes, even in \
the presence of a\\nnon-minimal coupling with the Ricci scalar which has a \
non-trivial profile. The\\nbackgrounds are planar and spherical black holes \
as well as solitons of\\n$SU\\\\left( 2\\\\right) \\\\times SU\\\\left( \
2\\\\right) $ $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ gauged\\nsupergravity in four dimensions. On \
these geometries, we compute the spectrum\\nof (quasi-)normal modes for the \
non-minimally coupled scalar field. We find\\nthat the equation for the \
radial dependence can be integrated in terms of\\nhypergeometric functions \
leading to an exact expression for the frequencies.\\nThe solutions do not \
asymptote to a constant curvature spacetime, nevertheless\\nthe asymptotic \
region acquires an extra conformal Killing vector. For the black\\nhole, the \
scalar probe is purely ingoing at the horizon, and requiring that \
the\\nsolutions lead to an extremum of the action principle we impose a \
Dirichlet\\nboundary condition at infinity. Surprisingly, the quasinormal \
modes do not\\ndepend on the radius of the black hole, therefore this family \
of geometries can\\nbe interpreted as isospectral in what regards to the wave \
operator\\nnon-minimally coupled to the Ricci scalar. We find both purely \
damped modes, as\\nwell as exponentially growing unstable modes depending on \
the values of the\\nnon-minimal coupling parameter. For the solitons we show \
that the same\\nintegrability property is achieved separately in a \
non-supersymmetric solutions\\nas well as for the supersymmetric one. \
Imposing regularity at the origin and a\\nwell defined extremum for the \
action principle we obtain the spectra that can\\nalso lead to purely \
oscillatory modes as well as to unstable scalar probes,\\ndepending on the \
values of the non-minimal coupling.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
