    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We compute the minimal area of a string worldsheet \
ending on two infinite\\nperiodic light-like Wilson lines in the AdS$_3$ \
boundary, which is dual to the\\nfirst non-planar correction to the gluon \
scattering amplitude in\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM at the strong coupling. \
Using the connection between the\\nHitchin system and the thermodynamic Bethe \
ansatz (TBA) equations, we present\\nan analytic method to compute the \
minimal area surface and express the\\nnon-trivial part of the minimal area \
in terms of the free energy of the\\nTBA-like equations. Given the cross \
ratios as inputs, the area computed from\\nthe TBA-like equations matches \
that calculated using the numerical integration.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
