   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2206.07720\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Matthew Dodelson\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Matthew Dodelson, Alba Grassi, Cristoforo Iossa, Daniel \
Panea Lichtig,\\n  and Alexander Zhiboedov\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Holographic thermal correlators from supersymmetric \
instantons\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"9 pages + appendices, 2 figures. v2: typos corrected, \
references\\n  added\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"SciPost Phys. 14, 116 (2023)\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.14.5.116\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"CERN-TH-2022-095\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We present an exact formula for the thermal scalar \
two-point function in\\nfour-dimensional holographic conformal field \
theories. The problem of finding\\nit reduces to the analysis of the wave \
equation on the AdS-Schwarzschild\\nbackground. The two-point function is \
computed from the connection coefficients\\nof the Heun equation, which can \
be expressed in terms of the\\nNekrasov-Shatashvili partition function of an \
SU(2) supersymmetric gauge theory\\nwith four fundamental hypermultiplets. \
The result is amenable to numerical\\nevaluation upon truncating the number \
of instantons in the convergent expansion\\nof the partition function. We \
also examine it analytically in various limits.\\nAt large spin the instanton \
expansion of the thermal two-point function\\ndirectly maps to the light-cone \
bootstrap analysis of the heavy-light\\nfour-point function. Using this \
connection, we compute the OPE data of\\nheavy-light double-twist operators. \
We compare our prediction to the\\nperturbative results available in the \
literature and find perfect agreement.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
