    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"On the convergence of Nekrasov functions\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"1+25 pages, comments welcome. v2 published \
version\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  In this note we present some results on the \
convergence of Nekrasov partition\\nfunctions as power series in the \
instanton counting parameter. We focus on\\n$U(N)$ ${\\\\mathcal N}=2$ gauge \
theories in four dimensions with matter in the\\nadjoint and in the \
fundamental representations of the gauge group respectively\\nand find \
rigorous lower bounds for the convergence radius in the two cases: if\\nthe \
theory is {\\\\it conformal}, then the series has at least a {\\\\it \
finite}\\nradius of convergence, while if it is {\\\\it asymptotically free} \
it has {\\\\it\\ninfinite} radius of convergence. Via AGT correspondence, \
this implies that the\\nrelated irregular conformal blocks of $W_N$ algebrae \
admit a power expansion in\\nthe modulus converging in the whole plane. By \
specifying to the $SU(2)$ case,\\nwe apply our results to analyse the \
convergence properties of the corresponding\\nPainlev\\\\'e \
$\\\\tau$-functions.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
