     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Matijn Fran\\\\c{c}ois\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Matijn Fran\\\\c{c}ois and Alba Grassi\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Painlev\\\\'e Kernels and Surface Defects at Strong \
Coupling\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Version 2: 50 pages, 1 figure. Minor corrections and \
clarifications,\\n  additional references. Comments welcome\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"Ann. Henri Poincar\\\\'e (2024)\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/s00023-024-01469-4\"\>"}], 
    ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"CERN-TH-2023-169\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th math-ph math.MP math.SP\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
    
    RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
     "\[Rule]", "\<\"  It is well established that the spectral analysis of \
canonically quantized\\nfour-dimensional Seiberg-Witten curves can be \
systematically studied via the\\nNekrasov-Shatashvili functions. In this \
paper, we explore another aspect of the\\nrelation between $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
supersymmetric gauge theories in four\\ndimensions and operator theory. \
Specifically, we study an example of an\\nintegral operator associated with \
Painlev\\\\'e equations and whose spectral\\ntraces are related to \
correlation functions of the 2d Ising model. This\\noperator does not \
correspond to a canonically quantized Seiberg-Witten curve,\\nbut its kernel \
can nevertheless be interpreted as the density matrix of an\\nideal Fermi \
gas. Adopting the approach of Tracy and Widom, we provide an\\nexplicit \
expression for its eigenfunctions via an $\\\\mathrm{O}(2)$ matrix \
model.\\nWe then show that these eigenfunctions are computed by surface \
defects in\\n$\\\\mathrm{SU}(2)$ super Yang-Mills in the self-dual phase of \
the\\n$\\\\Omega$-background. Our result also yields a strong coupling \
expression for\\nsuch defects which resums the instanton expansion. Even \
though we focus on one\\nconcrete example, we expect these results to hold \
for a larger class of\\noperators arising in the context of isomonodromic \
deformation equations.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Fri, 13 Oct 2023 17:20:47 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       
       RowBox[{"{", 
